## Why This Is Asked

Explores a practical, prefix-based data structure with duplicates, common in autocomplete and search features.

## Key Concepts

- Trie with per-node prefixCount and endCount
- Duplicate tracking via endCount
- Prefix-based queries in O(length(prefix))

## Code Example

```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.prefixCount = 0;
    this.endCount = 0;
  }
}
class Trie {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new TrieNode()); node = node.next.get(ch); node.prefixCount++; } node.endCount++; }
  erase(word) { if (!this.exists(word)) return false; let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { node = node.next.get(ch); node.prefixCount--; } node.endCount--; return true; }
  countWithPrefix(prefix) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of prefix) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return 0; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.prefixCount; }
  exists(word) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return false; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.endCount > 0; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you optimize memory for large, sparse alphabets?
- How would you extend to support deletion of all instances of a word efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement a compact prefix-based dictionary with duplicates and fast prefix queries using a Trie.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node counts; handling duplicates via passCount and endCount.
- Insert/erase adjust counts; erase stops if word not present.
- Prefix query is O(length(prefix)).

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode{ constructor(){ this.next=new Array(26).fill(null); this.pass=0; this.end=0; }}
class Trie{ constructor(){ this.root=new TrieNode(); }
 insert(w){ let p=this.root; for(const ch of w){ const i=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; if(!p.next[i]) p.next[i]=new TrieNode(); p=p.next[i]; p.pass++; } p.end++; }
 erase(w){ if(!this.contains(w)) return; let p=this.root; for(const ch of w){ const i=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; p=p.next[i]; p.pass--; } p.end--; }
 countPrefix(pfx){ let p=this.root; for(const ch of pfx){ const i=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; p=p.next[i]; if(!p) return 0; } return p.pass; }
 contains(w){ let p=this.root; for(const ch of w){ const i=ch.charCodeAt(0)-97; p=p.next[i]; if(!p) return false; } return p.end>0; }
 }
```

