## Why This Is Asked
- Introduces a practical autocomplete scenario and a foundational DS.
- Emphasizes handling duplicates and memory management.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node pass-through counts; O(length) ops; dynamic memory.
- Duplicate handling via cnt; pruning unused nodes to bound memory.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor(){ this.next = new Map(); this.cnt = 0; }
}
class Trie {
  constructor(){ this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word){ let node=this.root; for(let ch of word){ if(!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch,new TrieNode()); node = node.next.get(ch); node.cnt++; } }
  erase(word){ let stack=[]; let node=this.root; for(let ch of word){ if(!node.next.has(ch)) return; node = node.next.get(ch); stack.push([node,ch]); } // decrement
    for(let [nd] of stack){ nd.cnt--; }
  }
  countWithPrefix(prefix){ let node=this.root; for(let ch of prefix){ if(!node.next.has(ch)) return 0; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.cnt; }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of O(1) cache operations using standard data structures and eviction strategy. Emphasizes correct handling of updates, hits, and edge cases (capacity=1, missing keys).

## Key Concepts
- Hash map for O(1) lookups
- Doubly linked list for move-to-front in O(1)
- Eviction of least recently used on overflow
- Edge cases and empty states

## Code Example
```javascript
class LRUCache {
  constructor(capacity) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.map = new Map(); // key -> node
    this.head = null;
    this.tail = null;
  }
  _detach(node) {
    if (node.prev) node.prev.next = node.next; else this.head = node.next;
    if (node.next) node.next.prev = node.prev; else this.tail = node.prev;
  }
  _attachAtHead(node) {
    node.prev = null;
    node.next = this.head;
    if (this.head) this.head.prev = node;
    this.head = node;
    if (!this.tail) this.tail = node;
  }
  get(key) {
    const node = this.map.get(key);
    if (!node) return -1;
    this._detach(node);
    this._attachAtHead(node);
    return node.value;
  }
  put(key, value) {
    if (this.map.has(key)) {
      const node = this.map.get(key);
      node.value = value;
      this._detach(node);
      this._attachAtHead(node);
    } else {
      const node = { key, value, prev: null, next: null };
      this.map.set(key, node);
      this._attachAtHead(node);
      if (this.map.size > this.capacity) {
        // evict tail
        const oldTail = this.tail;
        this._detach(oldTail);
        this.map.delete(oldTail.key);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

